{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>He provoked His sons and daughters to anger.</b> This alludes to the First Temple, where the men and the women there served idolatry; as it is written (Jeremiah 44:9): ״השכחתם את רעות אבותיכם ואת רעות נשיכם״, and it is further written (Ezekiel 8:14): ״ויבא אותי אל פתח בית ה', והנה שם הנשים יושבות מבכות את התמוז״ — and this is the meaning of ״His sons and daughters״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:13.901014187Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}